  "verdict": "CLOSED-FORM DISC -23 & MASBAUM CYCLOTOMIC-ASYMMETRY ODD DATA DERIVED (scope-(a)/(b), zero free parameters, no parameter-free target match): (1) The 5_2 trace field K_{5_2} = Q(xi)/(xi^3 - 2*xi^2 + 3*xi - 1) ~ Q(z)/(z^3 - z^2 + 1) (via xi = 1 - z^2, z = -xi^2 + xi - 2) has disc -23 and quadratic resolvent Q(sqrt(-23)) (h(-23) = 3), disjoint from the retired Alexander-layer field Q(sqrt(-7)) (disc -7, h(-7) = 1). (2) Using the exact Bezout inverse 1/P'(xi_0) = (10*xi_0^2 - 17*xi_0 + 18)/23, every K_{5_2}-element alpha = a + b*xi + c*xi^2 has the closed-form bar-odd resolvent projection sigma_1(alpha) - sigma_2(alpha) = (((18*b + 26*c) - (17*b + 22*c)*xi_0 + (10*b + 17*c)*xi_0^2)/23)*sqrt(-23). At 1-loop (k=1), a factor of 23 cancels in the numerator, giving Delta_odd(P_1) = 11*(-10 + 7*xi_0 - 8*xi_0^2)/(4*23^2)*sqrt(-23) ~ -0.21114576*i. (3) On the Masbaum cyclotomic-coefficient side, C_{5_2,1}(q) = -(q^2 + q^4) has exact normalized bar-odd asymmetry ratio rho_1(q) = O_1(q^{-1})/E_1(q^{-1}) = (q^3 - q^{-3})/(q^3 + q^{-3}) = tanh(3*ln(q)) (~ 0.303185 at q_0), which is identically the H_3 bare content asymmetry x(c=3). (4) Neither the disc -23 resolvent odd datum nor the Masbaum cyclotomic asymmetry matches S_muon, S_proton, Im_Vb, or X_req without fitting.",
